astify/actions/runs/39249867214/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/actions/runs/39249867214/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/actions/runs/39249867214/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fastify/fastify/actions/workflows/40370","head_commit":{"id":"f5d01391e90b2e1d5d1c34a9d59ea529a10a55c3","tree_id":"335d377d1d1abdf85112cb9e989cffa8fb4c61af","message":"feat!: fail closed when a response content type is not declared in the content map\n\nWhen a route declares a per-media-type (`content`) response schema but the\nresponse `Content-Type` is neither a declared key nor `*/*`, the payload was\npreviously serialized with a raw `JSON.stringify`. That fallback bypassed the\nresponse schema and could expose fields the schema was meant to strip.\n\nThe route response path now fails closed. If the response content type is not\ndeclared and no `*/*` catch-all matches, `getSchemaSerializer` throws\n`FST_ERR_MISSING_CONTENTTYPE_SERIALIZATION_FN` and the reply is a `500`,\nsurfacing the misconfiguration instead of silently returning unsanitized data.\n\nThe error handler call path is unchanged: it still resolves the default error\nserializer (requesting `failClosed: false`), so error responses are unaffected.","timestamp":"2026-10-19T11:25:54Z","author":{"name":"Matteo Collina","email":"hello@matteocollina.com"},"committer":{"name":"Matteo Collina","email":"hello@matteocollina.com"}},"repository":{"id":69495170,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2OTQ5NTE3MA==","name":"fastify","full_name":"fastify/fastify","private":false,"owner":{"login":"fastify","id":24939410,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjI0OTM5NDEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24939410?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastify","html_url":"https://github.com/fastify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fastify/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/u